SUMMARY:Hammer Creek Bluegrass
DESCRIPTION:ONE SHOW ONLY — OCTOBER 23\, 2026\nWhether you’re a die-hard bluegrass fan or simply looking for a night of great live music\, Hammer Creek delivers the timeless songs of simpler days. Their music takes you back to the roots of bluegrass\, honoring legendary pioneers like Flatt & Scruggs\, The Stanley Brothers and Bill Monroe. With driving banjo\, heartfelt harmonies\, and that unmistakable high lonesome sound\, they bring this traditional American musical genre to life one song at a time. \nBased in Lancaster County\, Hammer Creek was formed in 2020 and have played shows throughout Pennsylvania\, Maryland and surrounding areas\, including the Buck Moon Bluegrass Festival\, the Appalachian Trail Music Festival and Fort Hunter Days. They have thrice been nominated for the Central Pennsylvania Music Award as Best Bluegrass Band. \nJoin us for a wholesome evening of traditional tunes and masterful musicianship. \nClick here for tickets.
URL:https://bird-in-hand.com/event/hammer-creek-bluegrass/
LOCATION:Bird-in-Hand Stage\, 2760 Old Philadelphia Pike #A\, Bird-in-Hand\, PA\, 17505\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bird-in-hand.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/HammerCreekHeader.jpg
GEO:40.0380988;-76.174466
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Bird-in-Hand Stage 2760 Old Philadelphia Pike #A Bird-in-Hand PA 17505 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2760 Old Philadelphia Pike #A:geo:-76.174466,40.0380988
